  "text": "Recipe: Quinoa Handvo \u2014 Air Fried\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Handvo\nIngredients: quinoa, seven different daals, methi dana (fenugreek seeds), water, bottle gourd, pumpkin, red onion, carrot, capsicum, beetroot, hing (asafoetida), black pepper, ginger, sweetener (dates | maple syrup), green chillies, pink salt, curry leaves, ENO, mustard seeds, cumin seeds, sesame seeds, crushed peanuts\nCooking methods: soak, grind, ferment, dry roast, saute, air-fry, microwave\nInstructions: BATTER:\n1 cup quinoa, 1 cup of seven different daals (beans of our choice), 1/2 tsp methi dana (fenugreek seeds) \u2014 soak overnight, rinse well, add 3 tsp water, grind it & keep for 6 to 8 hours for fermentation.\nPrepare 1.5 cups of grated mixed veggies of your choice. I used bottle gourd, pumpkin, red onion, carrot, capsicum, beetroot. Squeeze the juice out of grated veggies with hands to make them less watery \u2014 use this juice as a vegetable broth for another recipe.\nMix grated mixed vegetables with fermented batter. Add 1/4 tsp hing (asafoetida), 1/2 tsp black pepper, 1 inch ginger (grated), 1/2 tsp sweetener (dates | maple syrup), some green chillies (to taste), 1/4 tsp pink salt (to taste), a few drops of lemon juice, 3-4 curry leaves (minced). Finally add 1 tsp ENO just before cooking the batter.\nROASTED MASALA:\nDry roast mustard seeds, cumin seeds, curry leaves, sesame seeds and some crushed peanuts.\nDivide the batter into three equal portions.\nUTHAPAM STYLE HANDVO: Pour one portion of batter on non-stick pan. Prepare like uthapam. Garnish with roasted masala. Cook for 5 to 8 minutes on slow flame, covered with a lid. Then flip it over and cook for another 5 to 8 minutes.\nAIR FRIED HANDVO: Air fry the second portion of batter for 15 mins each side at 180 C.\nMICROWAVED HANDVO: Pour the third portion of batter into mugs. Microwave for 3 mins.\nNotes: Use this juice as a vegetable broth for another recipe.",
